  "description_html": "Size comparison of the five most complete abelisaurids. <i>Carnotaurus</i> and <i>Aucasaurus</i> are based on their respective skeletals by Scott Hartman (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://www.skeletaldrawing.com/theropods/carnotaurus\">[1]</a> &amp; <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://www.skeletaldrawing.com/theropods/aucasaurus\">[2]</a>), <i>Ekrixinatosaurus</i> is based on <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ekrixinatosaurus_novasi_skeletal_diagram.png\" title=\"File:Ekrixinatosaurus novasi skeletal diagram.png\">File:Ekrixinatosaurus novasi skeletal diagram.png</a>, and <i>Skorpiovenator</i> and <i>Majungasaurus</i> are based on <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Rafael_Delcourt/publication/307977647_Orlando_Grillo_Rafael_Delcourt/links/57d56fb808ae601b39aa6c54/Orlando-Grillo-Rafael-Delcourt.pdf\">Grillo &amp; Delcourt (2016)</a>. Human silhouette from <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silhouette_of_man_standing_and_facing_forward.svg\" title=\"File:Silhouette of man standing and facing forward.svg\">File:Silhouette of man standing and facing forward.svg</a>.",
